+ * the ring/crumbs at 0x882xxxxx likewise. No SCM/TrustZone buffers on this board. XNU runs on one core (CPU1 off),
+ * so the cacheable write-back IOSurface pages are only ever read by the same core. Tab 2 is excluded: its Cortex-A9
+ * has a PL310 outer cache that set/way operations do not reach. */
+/* Run 111: the ARM data cache was never enabled. The boot stub turns SCTLR.C off (XNU's locore wants caches off) and
+ * locore only turns the I-cache back on, so every load and store in the kernel and in every process went to RAM
+ * uncached: backboardd's software GL ran ~1000x slower than natively and the kernel needed ~200 ms to read one frame
+ * (runs 107-110). Nothing on this port reads RAM by DMA behind the CPU (the eMMC driver is PIO; the panel's
+ * framebuffer, the log ring and MMIO are mapped non-cacheable), kernel and user pages are write-through.
+ * While C is still 0 no line can hold newer data than RAM, so first invalidate every data/unified cache level by
+ * set/way (L1 and the Krait L2 may still hold stale lines from Android), then set C. */
